WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.931 --> 00:00:03.370
- [Shopper] Absolutely ridiculous.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.390
- [Reporter] A months-long shortage

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.100
of baby formula in the US,

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.390
caused by a mix of supply
chain issues and a recall,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.400
is putting desperate parents on edge

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.450
as they scramble to find
ways to feed their babies.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.250
- For those babies who
are not being breastfed

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.090
or otherwise getting human milk,

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.810
formula is the only alternative,

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.800
and it provides all of their nutrition.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.440
- [Reporter] So what can parents do now?

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.690
And more importantly,
what should they avoid?

00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:31.580
(mellow music)

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.680
- Definitely do not water it
down or make your own formula.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.740
These are dangerous

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.330
and there's simply no
safe way to do those.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:39.600
- [Reporter] Dr Steven Abrams,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.630
a former Chair of the
Committee on Nutrition

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.500
at the American Academy
of Pediatrics says that,

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.760
similar to breast milk,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.560
baby formula contains
protein and nutrients

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.420
that are crucial to a child's
development and growth,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.403
such as calcium,
phosphorus, iron, and zinc.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.300
- [Dr Abrams] When you make your own,

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.990
you can't get the nutrients right

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.140
and it's hard to do it in
a way that's sterile enough

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.700
to make sure that you're
not risking infection.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.960
When you dilute the formula,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.750
you're simply giving the baby extra water

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.010
that they don't need,

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.590
and they're filling up their
tummy with water and not food.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.681
It's what they need to grow.

00:01:11.681 --> 00:01:14.381
(mellow music)

00:01:14.381 --> 00:01:16.630
It's okay to switch baby formulas,

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.400
unless your baby has
special medical needs.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.490
- [Reporter] Experts say it's safe

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.070
for most healthy babies to switch

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:24.790
to any FDA-approved
formula parents can find

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.630
from reputable distributors.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.870
The American Academy of Pediatrics warns

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.030
against buying formulas on auction sites

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:34.360
that are not monitored
or regulated by the FDA.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.160
- [Dr Abrams] Babies who
have specialized problems,

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.840
especially those with severe allergies,

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.340
families need to talk
to their pediatrician

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.364
before they switch.

00:01:41.364 --> 00:01:44.200
(mellow music)

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.650
- [Reporter] As major
retailers like CVS, Walgreens,

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.670
Kroger and Target impose
purchase limits on baby formula

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.200
to avoid panic buying
and hoarding products,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.660
experts recommend checking
smaller local stores

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:55.970
and pharmacies.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.070
- I've seen it, for example,

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:59.980
in stores that only sell kosher food,

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.760
because they make the
specialized kosher formula.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.770
Sometimes you'll find it in smaller stores

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:09.027
that you might not expect to find it in.

00:02:09.027 --> 00:02:11.610
(mellow music)

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.350
- [Reporter] At least 31 milk
banks in the US and Canada

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.610
are collecting donations
from lactating women

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.540
and distributing pasteurized milk.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.373
These members of

00:02:21.373 --> 00:02:24.170
the Human Milk Banking
Association of North America

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.690
are currently helping families
facing difficulties due

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.230
to the formula shortage.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.650
- [Dr Abrams] The problem is that most

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.680
of that milk goes for premature babies,

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.940
so there isn't a whole lot
left for the general use,

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.193
but as long as the milk is
pasteurized, it's quite safe.

00:02:39.973 --> 00:02:41.870
(mellow music)

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.300
- [Reporter] Although the CDC says parents

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.500
who want to give their
children cow's milk should wait

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.730
until after the infant's first birthday,

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.420
Dr Abrams says this can
be a last resort option

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.290
for babies older than six
months, in case of an emergency.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.514
- For short periods of time,

00:02:54.514 --> 00:02:55.347
a week, two weeks of time,

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.570
you can use whole cow milk
if your baby's not allergic.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.190
- [Reporter] Dr Abrams
says parents should talk

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.580
to their pediatricians about
getting an iron supplement

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.460
for babies who are on cow's milk,

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.760
because whole cow milk is too low in iron

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.323
for the nutritional needs.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.270
The shortage, which stems

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.210
from pandemic-related supply issues,

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.090
worsened after Abbott Laboratories,

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.950
a major formula manufacturer,

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:21.780
voluntarily recalled some
products and closed a plant.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.820
On May 16, the company announced
that it had reached a deal

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:27.840
with the FDA for the reopening
of their formula plant,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.360
but a date has not yet been confirmed.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.460
On May 18, President Biden invoked

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.700
the Defense Production Act,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.200
to help manufacturers increase
production of baby formula.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.770
The administration also
launched a new program

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:41.360
that would use commercial aircrafts

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.960
to pick up overseas formula
that meets US standards.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.500
- I'm hopeful that the
government allowing imports

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.200
and increased production

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.540
will begin to see a turnaround
over the next couple weeks,

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.230
but I think we're still gonna
be need to be very careful.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.100
I don't expect to see full resolution

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.200
until, really, multiple months from now,

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.100
and families need to be aware of that.

